Bugs Found & Fixed (chronological)
blocked(m) scope bug (server) — a local function defined inside one function was called from a different function where it didn't exist, causing a silent runtime error that permanently broke scanWorkspaceVehicles() after the first time a player entered a vehicle. This was the original "planes never re-register after I enter a vehicle" bug. Fixed by replacing with the existing top-level isWorldModel().
Duplicate targetWhitelist table keys (client) — Lua silently uses the last value when a table literal has a duplicate key. Two spots had targetWhitelist = makeWhitelist(...) followed by targetWhitelist = table.clone(...), meaning the first was always dead code. Cleanup initially kept the wrong one, causing units to auto-authorize the ENTIRE target catalog by default (real regression, caught by user, reverted).
getHoverTarget() too narrow (client) — in-world click-to-tag only recognized models with Humanoid/Durability/Health/Arsenal children, missing vehicles that only had seats/FlightAI/etc. Broadened, then later made to check the CRAM_Vehicle CollectionService tag first (single source of truth matching what Live tab uses).
