Fundamental detection was heuristic/guessy — original code tried to infer "is this a vehicle" via structural heuristics (looking for Engine+unanchored parts, seat types, etc.) scanning the entire workspace recursively. This was fragile and caused Live tab / click-targeting to disagree with each other. Root architectural fix: built RadarAPI.
Global "ENGAGE ALL" / "IGNORE ALL" buttons were swapped (client) — ENGAGE ALL cleared the whitelist but never populated it (visually green, functionally empty = nothing authorized); IGNORE ALL populated the whitelist with everything (visually all off, functionally authorized everything). This was why the user saw completely inverted behavior. Fixed.
RadarAPI — Current Design (this is the core of the new architecture)

A profile-based module requiring in ServerScriptService, used by both the server controller and CIWS unit controller.

Detection (RadarAPI.scan()):

Scans children of any container literally named "Model" in workspace (Adonis's insert staging folder) AND workspace's own direct children (critical: confirmed via live trace logs that vehicles get reparented OUT of the Model staging folder to workspace root once they finish loading — this was the most recent real bug, now fixed)
Explicitly excludes anything named "Model" itself from being treated as a candidate (avoids the container being misclassified via recursive child search)
Caches results for 0.2s (RadarAPI._cacheTTL) to avoid re-scanning every call

Classification (RadarAPI.Profiles):

Helicopter — matches via Rotors/PilotSeat/RotorHitbox/BulletHitbox descendants
CombatJet — matches via Afterburner/MainParts descendants
Generic — fallback for anything else (ground vehicles etc.)
Order matters, first match wins (RadarAPI.ProfileOrder)

Damage model (confirmed against real vehicle structure):

Helicopters: reduce EVERY Durability NumberValue found on the model per hit (most helis have 2-3: tail rotor, main rotor, hull/bullet hitbox). Falls back to a single Health value for simpler helis if no Durability values exist.
Jets: drain Health (found under Plane submodel). On kill, set Crashed = true. Small chance (15%) per hit to knock out one currently-running StatusMain.ENGINE_LEFT/ENGINE_RIGHT/APU bool (confirmed semantics: true = running fine, false = damaged/failed). Important: Arsenal folder is ammo/weapon inventory counts (GAU8A, AIM9X, JDAMS, Rockets, Flares + Type strings), NOT damage flags — must never be touched by damage logic. This was a mistake I made and corrected mid-conversation.

Multi-system cooperation:

RadarAPI.registerSystem(name, settings) / unregisterSystem / getSystems() — any number of independent air-defense systems can register themselves
RadarAPI.claimTarget(systemName, targetPart) / releaseTarget(targetPart) — prevents two systems from double-locking the same target if you want that behavior
Designed so a second, entirely separate defense system (SAM site, flak battery, etc.) can require the same module and share detection/coordination without any code duplication

